    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0669" n="587" xml:id="pg587"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Romero</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-06"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March</hi> 15, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Sir: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of your communication of the
                    17th ultimo, in which you are pleased to communicate, for the information of the
                    government of the United States, a printed copy of the proclamation which the
                    constitutional President of the Mexican republic, his excellency Benito Juarez,
                    addressed to his fellow-countrymen on the 1st of January, 1865, and in which he
                    renews his determination to continue the struggle in Mexico in defence of the
                    liberty and independence of the republic.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for your polite attention in communicating to me so interesting a
                    document, I avail myself of the occasion to reiterate to you, sir, the
                    assurances of my very distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matias Romero, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
